Two more valid Codex P2s, both regressions against the ORIGINAL moveTab
behaviour that the dnd-kit rewrite quietly dropped. Worth noting the pattern:
every finding in this PR after the first has been 'the rewrite lost something
moveTab did'. When replacing a handler, diff its post-conditions, not just its
happy path.

1. Cancel restored the entire snapshot. If panes changed mid-drag the restore
   undid that too - handleProjectMutation removing a deleted project's tab was
   the concrete case, and cancelling resurrected it permanently. Now cancel
   repositions ONLY the dragged tab via movedToPane + applyTabGroups. That is
   safe because applyTabGroups maps ids through byId built from CURRENT panes,
   so an id that no longer exists is silently dropped - it cannot resurrect a
   tab even if the restore names it.
2. The source pane activated tabs[0]. moveTab uses
   remaining[Math.min(fromTabIndex, remaining.length - 1)]. Restored by
   recording the dragged tab's original index in  from the snapshot.

Test-writing traps hit here:
- A project tab needs path '/projects/<id>' to decorate as kind 'project'.
  '/agents/<id>' decorates as kind 'agent' titled 'Agent', so the deletion
  filter (tab.kind === 'project') never matched and my mid-drag assertion
  passed vacuously. describeWorkspacePath OVERWRITES the seeded kind/title, so
  seeding a kind directly does not work.
- Both new tests were confirmed to FAIL without their fix. The resurrection one
  shows 'Project' reappearing; the active-tab one picks 'New work' instead of
  'Projects'. Three tests in this PR would have been vacuous without that check.

